# Probe 33 (scripts/probe_apply_legend_totals.py): bp apply's own Legend column on clustered charts, legend off and table totals, nothing patched by hand, on the demo's model.
# Seen (bridge captures, then a real refresh + Ctrl+S): every visual drew as its probe-32 candidate did: Region legend side by side on the clustered column and bar (also beside a Country > Region drill-down with an Order Date legend), legend bottom and right, legend off hid the legend on a column, a bar and a line, legend top showed it on top, no option showed it at the bottom, totals "off" drew no Total row ("on" and no option drew Total 500); no error. The save raised 11 of the 15 data visuals' $schema 2.13.0 -> 2.14.0 and added condition-less auto filterConfigs (Categorical for columns, Advanced for measures); it also flipped the second drill level's `active` true -> false on the bar drill-down (drill view state). It changed no Series, legend or total property. Re-applying the specs changed nothing. Editing one chart's spec from legend off to top and re-applying removed `show` and wrote `position: 'Top'`; reloaded through the bridge, that chart drew its legend on top (the first capture right after the reload was blank, a mid-reload frame; the second drew every chart). All content invented.

